      objectReference: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e910c6af64194d44a9079d988104a9dd, type: 3}
    - target: {fileID: 7471192127214962485, guid: 5b2e4934ebd10e64287cb6b5cb5f75cd, type: 3}
      propertyPath: pages.Array.data[2].title
      value: Disconnected Wire
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7471192127214962485, guid: 5b2e4934ebd10e64287cb6b5cb5f75cd, type: 3}
      propertyPath: pages.Array.data[3].image
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e2d6cefeda6f60b4084ba667120a96c2, type: 3}
    - target: {fileID: 7471192127214962485, guid: 5b2e4934ebd10e64287cb6b5cb5f75cd, type: 3}
      propertyPath: pages.Array.data[3].title
      value: AND Gate
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7471192127214962485, guid: 5b2e4934ebd10e64287cb6b5cb5f75cd, type: 3}
      propertyPath: pages.Array.data[0].description
      value: The NOR gate is the opposite of the OR gate. It outputs 1 only when
        all inputs are 0. It is also a universal gate, meaning all other logic gates
        can be constructed using only NOR gates.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7471192127214962485, guid: 5b2e4934ebd10e64287cb6b5cb5f75cd, type: 3}
      propertyPath: pages.Array.data[1].description
      value: To connect the wire you have to trace it and just follow the path to
        reach the other end.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7471192127214962485, guid: 5b2e4934ebd10e64287cb6b5cb5f75cd, type: 3}
      propertyPath: pages.Array.data[2].description
      value: The wire will connect and glow after successfull tracing.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7471192127214962485, guid: 5b2e4934ebd10e64287cb6b5cb5f75cd, type: 3}
